From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:13:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: arm64: make bootm_size cover the load layout

bootm_size bounds where bootm may relocate the kernel, FDT and initrd.
At 160MB it is smaller than the layout below it, which places
RAMDISK_ADDR_R at 255MB. The boot script's scratch loads (armbianEnv.txt
and a DTB) are also reserved in LMB for the rest of the session, so the
window is fragmented further, and an 84MB initrd fails with
"ramdisk - allocation error". Use 512MB. LMB does not hand out absent
or reserved memory, so this is safe on smaller boards.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 include/configs/sunxi-common.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
index e92447c7..9dffad8d 100644
--- a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
+++ b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
  * for really big kernels, say 256MB for now.
  * Scripts, PXE and DTBs should go afterwards, leaving the rest for the initrd.
  */
-#define BOOTM_SIZE        __stringify(0xa000000)
+#define BOOTM_SIZE        __stringify(0x20000000)
 #define KERNEL_ADDR_R     __stringify(SDRAM_OFFSET(0080000))
 #define KERNEL_COMP_ADDR_R __stringify(SDRAM_OFFSET(4000000))
 #define KERNEL_COMP_SIZE  __stringify(0xb000000)
-- 
2.47.3

